Title: The sweep and the guard hook find the gate record of a forge merge by rebuilding the candidate from the merge's parents
Created: 2026-10-21
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-10-21T14:52Z reviewer created
2026-10-21T16:13Z reviewer reviewer note 2026-10-21 positive control run (criterion 1): after the first gated merge (PR 1596, merge commit 1b18e9e8, passing record on the candidate fb252e88), 'python3 scripts/main_sweep.py --repo . --max-count 4 --fetch' reports 1b18e9e8 as 'finding no-record', exactly like the three merges made before the gate (PRs 1568, 1569, 1599). So the mismatch is real: the sweep reads the note on the forge's merge commit, the record is on the deterministic candidate. Also: 'make main-sweep' (8-day range, one forge lookup per commit) did not finish in 200 s (rc 124) while --max-count 4 took 7 s, which supports deleting the forge-check path (the other 1179 criterion). Fix per this ticket: rebuild the candidate from the merge commit's two parents and read the note there.
2026-10-21T16:25Z reviewer reviewer note 2026-10-21 rescoped at the author's word: the audit is stateless, a 24-hour window, this repository only, git-only (forge path deleted), run from the lair wrap-up and by hand, never in the merge path. The watermark, tag and ref options are dropped; the 8-day rolling range and the activation-commit range are dropped. The candidate rebuild from the merge's parents stays (it is what lets any audit find a forge merge's receipt).

--- body ---
## Context
Found on 2026-10-21 by a read-only reading of tickets 1178 and 1156 with the design note
of PR 1588 and the merged code (reading, not yet run). The gate record is a git note on
the candidate commit: the `--no-ff` merge of the branch head into the base tip, built
deterministically with fixed metadata (`scripts/merge-gate.py`). The guard hook
(`hooks/reference-transaction`, PR 1566) and the sweep (`scripts/main_sweep.py`) look for a
note on the commit that actually enters `main`, with `git notes show <sha>`. When the
forge merges the pull request, the merge commit it creates is a different object from the
candidate (other author, date and message), so a gated merge that went through the forge
would carry no record on the commit the sweep reads: every gated merge reads "no record".
The two PRs were built in parallel against the agreed contract "note on the candidate
commit, ref `refs/notes/gate`", and the integration was never exercised.

Idea of the fix (the coder decides): for a merge commit M on `main` with parents (P1, P2),
rebuild the candidate from (P1, P2) with the same deterministic function and look the note up
there. That also gives the right answer when the base moved after the record was written
(the candidate of (new P1, P2) has no note: a stale record is a finding, as intended).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A positive control first, run before any change: take the first gated merge
      once the activation PR (1569) has landed, run `make main-sweep`, and record in the
      ticket log whether the sweep reads that merge as "gate record" or as a finding.
- [ ] If the mismatch is real: the sweep and the hook's gated-merge test rebuild the
      candidate from the merge commit's two parents and read the note there; one function
      builds the candidate, shared with `scripts/merge-gate.py` (no second implementation).
- [ ] Tests: a merge made with different metadata than the candidate (as the forge does) reads
      as gated when a record exists for (P1, P2); the same merge reads as a finding when the
      base moved (P1 differs) or no record exists; a fast-forward or single-parent commit is
      unchanged.
- [ ] The guard doc (`docs/2026-10-21-main-update-guard.md`) states how a forge merge is
      matched to its record.
- [ ] Rescoped by the author, 2026-10-21 ("stateless, window is 24 hours, scope is this repo"): the audit is a
      bounded daily check, not a standing sweep. `scripts/main_sweep.py` becomes git-only: delete the forge
      path (`GhForge`, `required_checks`, `check_conclusions`, `_checks_verdict`, the ruleset read, and their
      tests); no watermark, no stored state, no cron.
- [ ] Window: the merges that entered `main` in the last 24 hours (`--since "24 hours ago"`), with a hard
      commit cap and a time limit; hitting a cap prints that the range was cut and exits 2, never silent.
- [ ] Scope: this repository only, and only where the base declares a gate (`.merge-gate.json` present);
      otherwise the audit prints nothing.
- [ ] It never runs in the merge path (not in the gate's checks, not in the merge helper or recipe); it
      runs from `/lair`'s wrap-up as one line in the summary ("N merges in the last 24 h, M without a gate
      receipt: <first>") and by hand. The Makefile target and the cron example in the guard guide are
      removed or reduced to the 24 h window.
- [ ] Nothing here requires a particular agent runtime; PR under the 15-file breaker.
